#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096742 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096541 :question/id #uuid "b00f1213-cdaf-512c-9842-92cbee1ec63a" :question/math-academy-id "e-6100" :question/problem "Differentiate $y = \\cos^4{2x}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $y$ as a composite function\n\n$$\ny = u^4, \\qquad u = \\cos{v}, \\qquad v = 2x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d u} = 4u^3,\\qquad \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm d v} = -\\sin{v},\\qquad \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}v}{\\textrm d x} = 2.\n$$\n\nApplying now the chain rule twice, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}v}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =4{u}^{3}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡v)\\cdot (2) \\\\  & =4(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)^{3}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)\\cdot (2) \\\\  & =-8{cos}^{3}⁡2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f3ee0d5d-0821-5f6b-b613-6b814e65df50" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049332} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050271} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050789} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051084}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489452 :question-generator/id #uuid "9bf95cfb-a852-5313-852a-6ed5187445e3" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186096742.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097248 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dc9442cc-8d33-595e-9e41-73b4047b032d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9\\cos^{2} 3x\\sin 3x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095413} {:answer/id #uuid "fcdbd89b-535d-5d97-8858-715b0e7cbab2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9\\cos^{2} x\\sin x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095414} 