in x\\cos x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095423}] :answer-field/id #uuid "fa0a0398-2eac-50f7-a78d-91ba28b54adb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095418}] :question/id #uuid "bf61b2d5-63df-5002-abfc-0d0c2d68ffa6" :question/math-academy-id "q-48570" :question/problem "Find $f^{′}(x)$ when $f(x) = \\sin^{3} 4x$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233557 :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d32bf1a7-eae8-544d-b18f-ee99dc9e7258" :question/math-academy-id "q-16699" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{'}(1)$ when $f(x)={cos}^{3}(5{x}^{2}+2).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf={u}^{3},\\,u=\\operatorname{cos}v,\\,v=5{x}^{2}+2.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=3{u}^{2},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}v}=-\\operatorname{sin}v,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=10x.\n$$\n\nApplying now the chain rule twice, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}v}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =3{u}^{2}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}v)\\cdot 10x \\\\  & =3(\\operatorname{cos}(5{x}^{2}+2))^{2}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}(5{x}^{2}+2))\\cdot 10x \\\\  & =-30x{cos}^{2}(5{x}^{2}+2)\\operatorname{sin}(5{x}^{2}+2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we compute ${f}^{'}(1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{'}(1) & =-30(1){cos}^{2}(5(1)^{2}+2)\\operatorname{sin}(5(1)^{2}+2) \\\\  & =-30{cos}^{2}7\\operatorname{sin}7\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233782 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "584f034a-e243-5e92-85ec-d412187c42f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-120{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232542}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "584f034a-e243-5e92-85ec-d412187c42f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-120{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232542} :answer-field/id #uuid "abcda024-6128-542d-bc71-d5c1255b256a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232541}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d78ed24f-7cdd-50da-a7c5-8326d3933908" :question/math-academy-id "q-312907" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{'}(x)$ when $f(x)={cos}^{8}(5{x}^{3}).$\n\n${f}^{'}(x)=$\n{{field-1}} ${cos}^{7}(5{x}^{3})\\operatorname{sin}(5{x}^{3})$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf={u}^{8},\\,u=\\operatorname{cos}v,\\,v=5{x}^{3}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=8{u}^{7},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}v}=-\\operatorname{sin}v,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=15{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nApplying now the chain rule twice, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}v}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =8{u}^{7}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}v)\\cdot 15{x}^{2} \\\\  & =8{(\\operatorname{cos}(5{x}^{3}))}^{7}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}(5{x}^{3}))\\cdot 15{x}^{2} \\\\  & =-120{x}^{2}{cos}^{7}(5{x}^{3})\\operatorname{sin}(5{x}^{3}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290520 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f0c7111-a060-5641-9f28-08ebb3f97820" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "54x{sin}^{2}⁡(9{x}^{2}-1)\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(9{x}^{2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288462} {:answer/id #uuid "4bff2b13-d34a-5a2a-ab84-1110b5438aad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x{sin}^{2}⁡(9{x}^{2}-1)\\,{cos}^{2}⁡(9{x}^{2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288558} {:answer/id #uuid "9a36fc3b-3a7c-5fac-bbfb-9178461a03fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18x{sin}^{2}⁡(9{x}^{2}-1)\\,{cos}^{2}⁡(9{x}^{2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289063} {:answer/id #uuid "b0394bcf-fb4f-5bf6-9de5-f7e8cc6ee14a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18x{sin}^{2}⁡(9{x}^{2}-1)\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(9{x}^{2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289196} {:answer/id #uuid "d6add1df-78d9-5682-b6d5-4c7d9b74e6ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "54x{sin}^{3}⁡(9{x}^{2}-1)\\,{cos}^{3}⁡(9{x}^{2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289458}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f0c7111-a060-5641-9f28-08ebb3f97820" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "54x{sin}^{2}⁡(9{x}^{2}-1)\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(9{x}^{2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288462} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a37d7f9-8684-5d8d-b945-6f277a28d504" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289997}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d9cfcb56-203d-51a2-aa05-78075c70500a" :question/math-academy-id "q-2397" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ when $f(x)={sin}^{3}⁡(9{x}^{2}-1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf={u}^{3},\\,u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,v=9{x}^{2}-1.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=3{u}^{2},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}v}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=18x.\n$$\n\nApplying now the chain rule twice, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}v}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =3{u}^{2}\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡v)\\cdot 18x \\\\  & =3(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(9{x}^{2}-1))^{2}\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡(9{x}^{2}-1))\\cdot 18x \\\\  & =54x{sin}^{2}⁡(9{x}^{2}-1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(9{x}^{2}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297166 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0480da11-736f-54eb-8f1c-b45c5eafb77b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295288} {:answer/id #uuid "656e07a7-3c98-59bf-85d3-2d52b695e711" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295845} {:answer/id #uuid "9bf163c6-73b7-53e4-8558-870d5120e61c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296098} {:answer/id #uuid "a4e00c3b-4340-5c91-be7a-047cb1624ae3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296136} {:answer/id #uuid "c4fe8de4-4953-53e2-babf-0316522289bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296305}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0480da11-736f-54eb-8f1c-b45c5eafb77b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295288} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b048a01-7c6a-5074-8040-31f2a7ab3a71" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296859}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d0b4e552-dbf9-536f-981b-a75efbb821de" :question/math-academy-id "q-28655" :question/problem "Find ${h}^{′}(0)$ when $h(x)={5}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $h$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nh={5}^{u},\\,u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡v\\,v=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}u}={5}^{u}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}v}=\\frac{1}{v},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$\n\nApplying now the chain rule twice, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}v}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={5}^{u}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\cdot (\\frac{1}{v})\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x) \\\\  & ={5}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\cdot (\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x})\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x) \\\\  & =-{5}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we compute ${h}^{′}(0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{′}(0) & =-{5}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡0)}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\operatorname{tan}⁡0 \\\\  & =-{5}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5(0) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297370 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a923d0d-683f-5a22-8b67-4a4f6919866f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2(x+6){csc}^{2}⁡[(x+6)^{2}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295424} {:answer/id #uuid "272999f6-d0d3-5ba0-9d45-afe5af8fefcd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{csc}^{2}⁡[(x+6)^{2}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295481} {:answer/id #uuid "a23f01d4-b0cf-5d81-b3a4-2e37d3003baf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x{csc}^{2}⁡[(x+6)^{2}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296131} {:answer/id #uuid "ba4d398b-f413-539d-9058-6015c9708ad4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2(x+6)\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296244} {:answer/id #uuid "e1aa6a79-375b-56fc-a7eb-84281d9d15fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4(x+6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296469}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a923d0d-683f-5a22-8b67-4a4f6919866f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2(x+6){csc}^{2}⁡[(x+6)^{2}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295424} :answer-field/id #uuid "1cd72a85-2293-547b-8a73-3db56c2ab7b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296688}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8c9a1630-1e07-5782-a0c4-5e97e3d68c4f" :question/math-academy-id "q-31352" :question/problem "Find ${y}^{′}$ when $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡[(x+6)^{2}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{cot}⁡u,\\,u={v}^{2},\\,v=x+6.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=-{csc}^{2}⁡u,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}v}=2v,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=1.\n$$\n\nApplying now the chain rule twice, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}v}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =-{csc}^{2}⁡u\\cdot (2v)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-2(x+6){csc}^{2}⁡[(x+6)^{2}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297371 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "143d951a-1e7a-598c-ab01-6ac4eebb972d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20{cot}^{3}⁡1{csc}^{2}⁡1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295381} {:answer/id #uuid "80ac022d-2fa2-5312-b6bb-20edccc427c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{cot}^{3}⁡1{sec}^{2}⁡1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295959} {:answer/id #uuid "cfd53f52-57a0-58c2-84e5-51e7836dcaa8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4{cot}^{2}⁡1{csc}^{2}⁡1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296358} {:answer/id #uuid "df819a99-e827-5e8d-8038-4bdc1f81e2b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20\\operatorname{cot}⁡1{sec}^{2}⁡1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296451} {:answer/id #uuid "f7c37201-fff5-5a86-9be9-3c9d741d2eaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4{cot}^{3}⁡1{csc}^{2}⁡1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296584}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "143d951a-1e7a-598c-ab01-6ac4eebb972d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20{cot}^{3}⁡1{csc}^{2}⁡1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295381} :answer-field/id #uuid "c18783dd-cacf-52c8-94df-17f7aaad8258" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297033}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "60550674-e8b4-5f20-9b57-5b71c82e6894" :question/math-academy-id "q-31361" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{′}(0)$ when $f(x)={cot}^{4}⁡(5x-1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf={u}^{4},\\,u=\\operatorname{cot}⁡v,\\,v=5x-1.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=4{u}^{3},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}v}=-{csc}^{2}⁡v,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=5.\n$$\n\nApplying now the chain rule twice, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}v}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =4{u}^{3}\\cdot (-{csc}^{2}⁡v)\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =4(\\operatorname{cot}⁡(5x-1))^{3}\\cdot (-{csc}^{2}⁡(5x-1))\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =-20{cot}^{3}⁡(5x-1){csc}^{2}⁡(5x-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we compute ${f}^{′}(0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(0) & =-20{cot}^{3}⁡(5(0)-1){csc}^{2}⁡(5(0)-1) \\\\  & =-20{cot}^{3}⁡(-1){csc}^{2}⁡(-1) \\\\  & =-20(-{cot}^{3}⁡1){csc}^{2}⁡1 \\\\  & =20{cot}^{3}⁡1{csc}^{2}⁡1\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317339 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d3d2230-dda0-54b6-89ba-24372639fa9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}(2x-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315198}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0d3d2230-dda0-54b6-89ba-24372639fa9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}(2x-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315198} :answer-field/id #uuid "72951b74-10fa-525b-ae61-0c5a5cf05a42" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316821}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2c163105-12ab-5d59-bb79-bbc5b4799b09" :question/math-academy-id "q-342927" :question/problem "Find ${y}^{′}$ when $y=\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x-1)}.$\n\n| ${y}^{′}$ | $=$ | {{field-1}} |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | $\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x-1)}$ |" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt{u},\\,u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,v=2x-1.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}v}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=2.\n$$\n\nApplying now the chain rule twice, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}v}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡v)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x-1)}}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-1))\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-1)}{2\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x-1)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x-1)}{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x-1)}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489390 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30e7b9d4-67a3-5775-a5d2-ca4446d5b44e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\sin^{2} 4x\\cos 4x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489397} {:answer/id #uuid "59290209-9482-50f4-9098-13bb16954c34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12\\cos^{2} x\\sin x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489406} {:answer/id #uuid "80239181-a206-540d-80dd-4c77a3b494f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\sin^{2} 4x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489417} {:answer/id #uuid "dac562ba-737c-5fb3-9e6d-34d15181372b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12\\cos^{2} 4x\\sin 4x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489437} {:answer/id #uuid "f14bda28-1914-5bb5-b3c9-d58a85885cd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\cos^{2} 4x\\sin 4x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489447}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dac562ba-737c-5fb3-9e6d-34d15181372b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12\\cos^{2} 4x\\sin 4x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489437} :answer-field/id #uuid "031b15e0-3048-56cd-bce5-35907b4c2ec6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489389}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0b547b24-9888-53eb-ab95-e124d3f31432" :question/problem "Find $f^{′}(x)$ when $f(x) = \\cos^{3} 4x$." :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf=u^3,\\,u=\\cos v,\\,v=4x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}u}=3u^2,\\quad \\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}v}=-\\sin v,\\quad \\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}=4.\n$$\n\nApplying now the chain rule twice, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f'(x)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}u}\\cdot\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}v}\\cdot\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\\\\n&=3u^2\\cdot (-\\sin v)\\cdot 4\\\\\n&=-12\\cos^{2} 4x\\sin 4x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489392 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ac2a3d6-1261-55ae-9429-ab0a45e319bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6x{sin}^{3}⁡(1{x}^{2}-1)\\,{cos}^{3}⁡(1{x}^{2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489395} {:answer/id #uuid "3979ed87-af85-57db-8316-21223ec16943" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x{sin}^{2}⁡(1{x}^{2}-1)\\,{cos}^{2}⁡(1{x}^{2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489399} {:answer/id #uuid "5326b014-bdff-590c-91fd-da791559ff94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x{sin}^{2}⁡(1{x}^{2}-1)\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1{x}^{2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489405} {:answer/id #uuid "e2c86454-1fbf-57d8-9fab-f0e9a82e9af9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x{sin}^{2}⁡(1{x}^{2}-1)\\,{cos}^{2}⁡(1{x}^{2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489443} {:answer/id #uuid "f7dc7484-013b-5097-9937-5df5cca67819" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6x{sin}^{2}⁡(1{x}^{2}-1)\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1{x}^{2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489449}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f7dc7484-013b-5097-9937-5df5cca67819" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6x{sin}^{2}⁡(1{x}^{2}-1)\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1{x}^{2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489449} :answer-field/id #uuid "a31723c2-df16-5a29-a9cf-4ab545f80f99" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489424}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2168b13d-cc27-5e92-a481-beee5381eccc" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ when $f(x)={sin}^{3}⁡(1{x}^{2}-1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf={u}^{3},\\,u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,v=1{x}^{2}-1.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=3{u}^{2},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}v}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=2x.\n$$\n\nApplying now the chain rule twice, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}v}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =3{u}^{2}\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡v)\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =3(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1{x}^{2}-1))^{2}\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1{x}^{2}-1))\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =6x{sin}^{2}⁡(1{x}^{2}-1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1{x}^{2}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489410 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "645f8651-c907-5897-a0f8-5495b4696424" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9\\sin 3x\\cos 3x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489409} {:answer/id #uuid "88fccb2c-a82c-5005-b096-ec2ab5d38a68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9\\sin^{2} x\\cos x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489420} {:answer/id #uuid "e4660400-a1f8-5409-a2f2-c6cebf3a25e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sin^{2} 3x\\cos 3x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489444} {:answer/id #uuid "e9377be7-0c61-5ada-a744-bc51453850a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sin x\\cos x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489446} {:answer/id #uuid "feca9f99-8e26-59c1-8151-7e33c2d68ee2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9\\sin^{2} 3x\\cos 3x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489451}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "feca9f99-8e26-59c1-8151-7e33c2d68ee2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9\\sin^{2} 3x\\cos 3x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489451} :answer-field/id #uuid "7eb18e9f-7b04-574c-bf8c-fb35e930eba6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489416}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "69eb6901-57ef-5c23-9e79-478c120da8a0" :question/problem "Find $f^{′}(x)$ when $f(x) = \\sin^{3} 3x$." :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf=u^3,\\,u=\\sin v,\\,v=3x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}u}=3u^2,\\quad \\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}v}=\\cos v,\\quad \\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}=3.\n$$\n\nApplying now the chain rule twice, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f'(x)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}u}\\cdot\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}v}\\cdot\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\\\\n&=3u^2\\cdot (\\cos v)\\cdot 3\\\\\n&=9\\sin^{2} 3x\\cos 3x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489415 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1578d2e7-e3c7-58ca-ae2c-e000eee7b584" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6\\cos^{2} x\\sin x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489391} {:answer/id #uuid "31dbc390-d7ff-52b7-9554-7039ff3e33a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\sin^{2} 2x\\cos 2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489398} {:answer/id #uuid "a6daa534-1144-57a1-bda8-9347e8f3c975" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\cos^{2} 2x\\sin 2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489425} {:answer/id #uuid "ba9b90a3-6e76-58c1-b372-848a72b05143" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\sin^{2} 2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489428} {:answer/id #uuid "e071ac82-c30e-510e-891d-7e6d4aab4fa3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6\\cos^{2} 2x\\sin 2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489438}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e071ac82-c30e-510e-891d-7e6d4aab4fa3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6\\cos^{2} 2x\\sin 2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489438} :answer-field/id #uuid "e16ae766-5a2f-5472-aaef-e0f1cfc54863" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489440}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "78f271bc-8d43-5a38-8524-01c52619086f" :question/problem "Find $f^{′}(x)$ when $f(x) = \\cos^{3} 2x$." :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf=u^3,\\,u=\\cos v,\\,v=2x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}u}=3u^2,\\quad \\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}v}=-\\sin v,\\quad \\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}=2.\n$$\n\nApplying now the chain rule twice, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f'(x)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}u}\\cdot\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}v}\\cdot\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\\\\n&=3u^2\\cdot (-\\sin v)\\cdot 2\\\\\n&=-6\\cos^{2} 2x\\sin 2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489427 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e198e28-7ad4-54be-9fe1-0ede79594f34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\sin^{2} 2x\\cos 2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489401} {:answer/id #uuid "6b326e02-a18a-5405-9760-a7eadc21044f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sin x\\cos x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489411} {:answer/id #uuid "8aa31131-7bc2-5861-b733-db93afc59ee7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sin^{2} 2x\\cos 2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489421} {:answer/id #uuid "e0fffbf4-1840-5e14-8dd6-a5d71b97666c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\sin 2x\\cos 2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489439} {:answer/id #uuid "e1e13535-c174-5ff3-a658-d532f5876d18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\sin^{2} x\\cos x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489441}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e198e28-7ad4-54be-9fe1-0ede79594f34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\sin^{2} 2x\\cos 2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489401} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb2277f3-ece1-5aa4-a6b5-143a44b7c878" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489435}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b67a6cf9-dc23-5ea7-a514-a5dcfabdbd86" :question/problem "Find $f^{′}(x)$ when $f(x) = \\sin^{3} 2x$." :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf=u^3,\\,u=\\sin v,\\,v=2x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}u}=3u^2,\\quad \\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}v}=\\cos v,\\quad \\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}=2.\n$$\n\nApplying now the chain rule twice, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f'(x)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}u}\\cdot\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}v}\\cdot\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\\\\n&=3u^2\\cdot (\\cos v)\\cdot 2\\\\\n&=6\\sin^{2} 2x\\cos 2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489430 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c23db35-1c82-59b5-adbb-2c1801e613c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8{cot}^{3}⁡1{csc}^{2}⁡1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489407} {:answer/id #uuid "607877ee-30d1-5662-a148-072bd2a65e8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\operatorname{cot}⁡1{sec}^{2}⁡1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489408} {:answer/id #uuid "6fbdb636-8a72-52ec-ab3b-ff891686c910" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4{cot}^{3}⁡1{csc}^{2}⁡1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489413} {:answer/id #uuid "868c8189-a478-5120-ad8e-fdc97fe80ed5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4{cot}^{2}⁡1{csc}^{2}⁡1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489419} {:answer/id #uuid "c4041f6b-566b-50c0-84f6-8e034c917e79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{cot}^{3}⁡1{sec}^{2}⁡1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489431}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c23db35-1c82-59b5-adbb-2c1801e613c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8{cot}^{3}⁡1{csc}^{2}⁡1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489407} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ee0f43d-3c4a-51a8-975c-eb46b3a70f21" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489402}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c3baed33-1cfd-5982-8e88-c33747aa34cf" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{′}(0)$ when $f(x)={cot}^{4}⁡(2x-1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf={u}^{4},\\,u=\\operatorname{cot}⁡v,\\,v=2x-1.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=4{u}^{3},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}v}=-{csc}^{2}⁡v,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=2.\n$$\n\nApplying now the chain rule twice, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}v}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =4{u}^{3}\\cdot (-{csc}^{2}⁡v)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =4(\\operatorname{cot}⁡(2x-1))^{3}\\cdot (-{csc}^{2}⁡(2x-1))\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-8{cot}^{3}⁡(2x-1){csc}^{2}⁡(2x-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we compute ${f}^{′}(0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(0) & =-8{cot}^{3}⁡(2(0)-1){csc}^{2}⁡(2(0)-1) \\\\  & =-8{cot}^{3}⁡(-1){csc}^{2}⁡(-1) \\\\  & =-8(-{cot}^{3}⁡1){csc}^{2}⁡1 \\\\  & =8{cot}^{3}⁡1{csc}^{2}⁡1\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489432 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2970eeb1-3b49-50db-9453-4ae0d788a789" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\operatorname{cot}⁡1{sec}^{2}⁡1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489394} {:answer/id #uuid "83cf7332-9e22-5d6b-ac71-dbdbc51417e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{cot}^{3}⁡1{sec}^{2}⁡1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489418} {:answer/id #uuid "c620ccb3-5b19-5217-abfc-3a07d7d021d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12{cot}^{3}⁡1{csc}^{2}⁡1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489434} {:answer/id #uuid "d7a96852-18db-5426-80b3-8889b50de605" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4{cot}^{2}⁡1{csc}^{2}⁡1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489436} {:answer/id #uuid "e235745d-204e-54fb-993d-8da177d2d7b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4{cot}^{3}⁡1{csc}^{2}⁡1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489442}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c620ccb3-5b19-5217-abfc-3a07d7d021d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12{cot}^{3}⁡1{csc}^{2}⁡1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489434} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe24ada9-bd92-5b0d-bbee-0258963f8532" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489450}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c51262c0-6413-5083-b852-6971681819a1" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{′}(0)$ when $f(x)={cot}^{4}⁡(3x-1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf={u}^{4},\\,u=\\operatorname{cot}⁡v,\\,v=3x-1.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=4{u}^{3},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}v}=-{csc}^{2}⁡v,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=3.\n$$\n\nApplying now the chain rule twice, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}v}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =4{u}^{3}\\cdot (-{csc}^{2}⁡v)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =4(\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x-1))^{3}\\cdot (-{csc}^{2}⁡(3x-1))\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =-12{cot}^{3}⁡(3x-1){csc}^{2}⁡(3x-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we compute ${f}^{′}(0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(0) & =-12{cot}^{3}⁡(3(0)-1){csc}^{2}⁡(3(0)-1) \\\\  & =-12{cot}^{3}⁡(-1){csc}^{2}⁡(-1) \\\\  & =-12(-{cot}^{3}⁡1){csc}^{2}⁡1 \\\\  & =12{cot}^{3}⁡1{csc}^{2}⁡1\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489445 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "420bec15-5b1c-5a49-848e-cd7d88c0122d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\cos^{2} 5x\\sin 5x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489403} {:answer/id #uuid "51162c0e-e911-55b6-b2f6-ee71df4f9905" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15\\cos^{2} x\\sin x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489404} {:answer/id #uuid "9c33688a-a6ce-5589-b010-ce864fe74a52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15\\cos^{2} 5x\\sin 5x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489423} {:answer/id #uuid "c14927a1-839b-53c3-a003-77536cb03a57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\sin^{2} 5x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489429} {:answer/id #uuid "c5e322d2-fdf0-5a97-8851-f93a72dcad20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15\\sin^{2} 5x\\cos 5x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489433}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9c33688a-a6ce-5589-b010-ce864fe74a52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15\\cos^{2} 5x\\sin 5x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489423} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c1f8536-cd5e-57c1-98bd-f1d312bce9b1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489412}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e7f20887-76fb-5d13-bcfc-20da4d07fad6" :question/problem "Find $f^{′}(x)$ when $f(x) = \\cos^{3} 5x$." :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf=u^3,\\,u=\\cos v,\\,v=5x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}u}=3u^2,\\quad \\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}v}=-\\sin v,\\quad \\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}=5.\n$$\n\nApplying now the chain rule twice, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f'(x)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}u}\\cdot\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}v}\\cdot\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\\\\n&=3u^2\\cdot (-\\sin v)\\cdot 5\\\\\n&=-15\\cos^{2} 5x\\sin 5x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489448 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22005ee4-41d0-5760-b893-f0fac19db39a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4{cot}^{3}⁡1{csc}^{2}⁡1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489393} {:answer/id #uuid "2f2a9975-b462-5030-bd6f-57419893c0e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1{cot}^{3}⁡1{sec}^{2}⁡1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489396} {:answer/id #uuid "6fd77f99-da27-58dd-a347-1c31d50cedc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{cot}^{3}⁡1{csc}^{2}⁡1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489414} {:answer/id #uuid "9249d26c-d661-549a-91a4-caf233a82221" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4{cot}^{2}⁡1{csc}^{2}⁡1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489422} {:answer/id #uuid "af8ef9cf-cd77-54c5-ad2b-ba9478fe6d6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{cot}⁡1{sec}^{2}⁡1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489426}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6fd77f99-da27-58dd-a347-1c31d50cedc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{cot}^{3}⁡1{csc}^{2}⁡1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489414} :answer-field/id #uuid "3abb3881-a4da-56ea-afd6-a57f4bafd656" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489400}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f751f15c-49b5-572a-960c-e6e9fe0fd73f" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{′}(0)$ when $f(x)={cot}^{4}⁡(1x-1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf={u}^{4},\\,u=\\operatorname{cot}⁡v,\\,v=1x-1.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=4{u}^{3},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}v}=-{csc}^{2}⁡v,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=1.\n$$\n\nApplying now the chain rule twice, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}v}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =4{u}^{3}\\cdot (-{csc}^{2}⁡v)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =4(\\operatorname{cot}⁡(1x-1))^{3}\\cdot (-{csc}^{2}⁡(1x-1))\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-4{cot}^{3}⁡(1x-1){csc}^{2}⁡(1x-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we compute ${f}^{′}(0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(0) & =-4{cot}^{3}⁡(1(0)-1){csc}^{2}⁡(1(0)-1) \\\\  & =-4{cot}^{3}⁡(-1){csc}^{2}⁡(-1) \\\\  & =-4(-{cot}^{3}⁡1){csc}^{2}⁡1 \\\\  & =4{cot}^{3}⁡1{csc}^{2}⁡1\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Derivative Using Multiple Instances of the Chain Rule"}]}
